Tips for Exercising During Your Period
Choose Comfortable Clothing

Wear breathable and comfortable clothes that allow you to move freely.

Carry Extra Pads

Always keep additional sanitary pads in your gym or sports bag.

Change Before Exercise

Starting your workout with a fresh pad can improve comfort.

Choose Activities That Feel Right

Walking, stretching, yoga, or other moderate activities may feel more comfortable for some people, while others may prefer their usual routine.

Stay Hydrated

Drink enough fluids throughout the day.

When Should You Take a Break?

If you feel unusually weak, dizzy, severely uncomfortable, or unwell, stop exercising and take care of yourself. Persistent or unusually heavy menstrual bleeding should be discussed with a healthcare professional.

Conclusion

Your period does not have to prevent you from staying active. Choose activities that feel comfortable and use menstrual protection suitable for your flow.

